public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.DGLocalSystem.CircleResolution
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.DGLocalSystem.Path.From

/-!
# Brown's resolution of a circle maps quasi-isomorphically to the chains on its based paths

For a Moore loop `γ` at `b`, the free module `K = C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₁` of
`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`, with `D e₁ = ([γ] - [1]) e₀`, is Brown's semi-free resolution of
`R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` for a circle with one `0`-cell at `b` and one `1`-cell attached along
`γ` (`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`). Brown's
construction compares such a module with the chains `C_*(P_b B; R)` on the Moore paths from `b`, a
differential graded left module over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` through concatenation in front
(`TauCeti.pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule`), by a map that is linear over the loop algebra: the
generator of each cell goes to a chain of paths whose boundary is the image of its attaching row.
This file constructs that comparison for the circle and proves that it is a quasi-isomorphism.

* The generator `e₀` of the `0`-cell goes to the point chain `[b]` of the constant path of length
  zero at `b`.
* The generator `e₁` of the `1`-cell goes to the `1`-chain `c_γ` of the initial segments of `γ`
  (`TauCeti.loopCellPathCube`): at time `s` the path `γ` truncated at `(1 - s)` times its length,
  through the contraction `TauCeti.MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy` of the based path space. Its
  boundary is `[γ] - [b]` (`TauCeti.loopCellPathChain_differential`), and since loops act on paths
  by concatenation in front this is `([γ] - [1]) · [b]`, the image of the row of `e₁`.

So the map `α e₀ + β e₁ ↦ α · [b] + β · c_γ` (`TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison`) commutes with the
differentials (`TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison_differential`), for every Moore loop `γ` of every
space, and it commutes with the augmentations
(`TauCeti.cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathComparison`).

When `B` is aspherical at `b` and the class of `γ` generates an infinite cyclic fundamental group,
as for a circle and a loop going once around it, both augmentations are quasi-isomorphisms onto
`R`: the based path space is contractible
(`TauCeti.exists_pathFromChainDifferential_eq_of_augmentation_eq_zero`), and `K` is Brown's
resolution. Hence so is the comparison
(`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq`), in the form
used for the attachment of cells
(`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.exists_attach_of_forall_exists`): every relative cycle
`(u, w)`, with `D u = 0` and `c(u) = d w`, is a relative boundary `(D u', c(u') + d w')`. The
case of the complex unit circle and its counterclockwise loop is
`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq`.

This is the circle instance of the comparison between Brown's semi-free model and the chains on
the based path space, whose general cell-by-cell construction runs along the skeletal filtration
`TauCeti.pathFromChainSkeleton`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.loopCellPathCube`: the `1`-cube of initial segments of a Moore loop, in `P_b B`.
* `TauCeti.loopCellPathChain`: its chain `c_γ`.
* `TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison`: the map `K → C_*(P_b B; R)`, linear over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.loopCellPathChain_differential`: `d c_γ = [γ] - [b]`.
* `TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison_differential`: the comparison commutes with the differentials.
* `TauCeti.cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathComparison`: it commutes with the
  augmentations.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq`: over an
  aspherical space whose fundamental group is infinite cyclic, generated by the class of `γ`, the
  comparison is a quasi-isomorphism.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq`: the
  case of the circle.

## References

* E. H. Brown, *Twisted tensor products, I*, Ann. of Math. (2) 69 (1959), 223–246.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, §1.4.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Morse homology with differential graded
  coefficients*, Progress in Mathematics 360, Birkhäuser, 2025, Chapters 3--4.
-/

public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicTopology

open scoped Topology unitInterval

namespace TauCeti

open NormalizedCubicalChain

section Comparison

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B}

/-- The `1`-cube of **initial segments of a Moore loop** `γ` at `b`, in the based path space
`P_b B`: at time `s` it is `γ`, read as a path from `b`, truncated at `(1 - s)` times its length.
It runs from `γ` to the constant path of length zero at `b`. -/
def loopCellPathCube (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) : SingularCube (MoorePathFrom B b) 1 :=
  ⟨fun x ↦ MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy (σ (x 0), γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b), by fun_prop⟩

theorem loopCellPathCube_apply (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (x : Fin 1 → I) :
    loopCellPathCube γ x = MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy (σ (x 0), γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The face of `TauCeti.loopCellPathCube γ` at time `0` is the loop `γ`, read as a path from
`b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem face_zero_zero_loopCellPathCube (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    SingularCube.face 0 0 (loopCellPathCube γ) =
      SingularCube.point (γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b) :=
  ContinuousMap.ext fun x ↦ by simp [SingularCube.face_apply, loopCellPathCube_apply]

/-- The face of `TauCeti.loopCellPathCube γ` at time `1` is the constant path of length zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem face_zero_one_loopCellPathCube (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    SingularCube.face 0 1 (loopCellPathCube γ) = SingularCube.point (MoorePathFrom.refl B b) :=
  ContinuousMap.ext fun x ↦ by simp [SingularCube.face_apply, loopCellPathCube_apply]

variable (H : Type*) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

variable (B b) in
/-- The point chain `[b]` of the constant path of length zero at `b`, in `C_*(P_b B; R)`. -/
def pathFromReflChain : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R :=
  cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0 (ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (MoorePathFrom.refl B b)))

/-- The `1`-chain `c_γ` of the initial segments of a Moore loop `γ`
(`TauCeti.loopCellPathCube`), in `C_*(P_b B; R)`. -/
def loopCellPathChain (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R :=
  cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 1 (ofCube _ R (loopCellPathCube γ))

variable {H R}

/-- The point chain `[b]` is a cycle. -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleDifferential_pathFromReflChain :
    cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (pathFromReflChain B b H R) = 0 :=
  cubicalChainModuleDifferential_lof_zero _

/-- The augmentation of the point chain `[b]` is `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_pathFromReflChain :
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (pathFromReflChain B b H R) = 1 := by
  rw [pathFromReflChain, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_lof_zero, augment_ofCube]

/-- The augmentation of `c_γ` vanishes, since it is a `1`-chain. -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathChain (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopCellPathChain H R γ) = 0 :=
  cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_lof_succ 0 _

/-- A loop chain acts on the point chain `[b]` by acting on the constant path: the point chain of a
loop `ω` takes `[b]` to the point chain of `ω`, read as a path from `b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem point_smul_pathFromReflChain (ω : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 (ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point ω)) •
        pathFromReflChain B b H R =
      cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0
        (ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (ω • MoorePathFrom.refl B b))) := by
  rw [pathFromReflChain, lof_smul_cubicalChainModuleLof, leftAct_ofCube]
  exact congrArg _ (congrArg _ (ContinuousMap.ext fun _ ↦ by
    rw [ContinuousMap.comp_apply, leftActMap_apply, SingularCube.crossProduct_apply,
      SingularCube.point_apply, SingularCube.point_apply, SingularCube.point_apply]))

/-- **The boundary of the initial segments of a loop**: `d c_γ = [γ] - [b]`, where `[γ]` is the
point chain of `γ`, read as a path from `b`. -/
theorem loopCellPathChain_differential (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopCellPathChain H R γ) =
      cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0 (ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b))) -
        pathFromReflChain B b H R := by
  rw [loopCellPathChain, cubicalChainModuleDifferential_lof_succ, boundary_ofCube,
    Fin.sum_univ_one, face_zero_zero_loopCellPathCube, face_zero_one_loopCellPathCube,
    Fin.val_zero, pow_zero, one_smul, map_sub, pathFromReflChain]

variable (H R) in
/-- **The comparison of Brown's resolution of a circle with the chains on its based paths**: the
map from the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` to `C_*(P_b B; R)`, linear over the loop
algebra `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`, sending the generator `e₀` of the `0`-cell to the point chain `[b]` of the
constant path and the generator `e₁` of the `1`-cell to the chain `c_γ` of the initial segments of
`γ`. -/
def loopCellPathComparison (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[loopChainAlgebra B b R]
      cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R :=
  Finsupp.linearCombination _
    (Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ pathFromReflChain B b H R) (fun _ ↦ loopCellPathChain H R γ))

@[simp]
theorem loopCellPathComparison_single_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (α : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellPathComparison H R γ (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α) =
      α • pathFromReflChain B b H R := by
  simp [loopCellPathComparison]

@[simp]
theorem loopCellPathComparison_single_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (β : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellPathComparison H R γ (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β) =
      β • loopCellPathChain H R γ := by
  simp [loopCellPathComparison]

/-- The comparison on `α e₀ + β e₁` is `α · [b] + β · c_γ`. -/
theorem loopCellPathComparison_apply (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellPathComparison H R γ u =
      u (Sum.inl ()) • pathFromReflChain B b H R + u (Sum.inr ()) • loopCellPathChain H R γ := by
  have hu : u = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (u (Sum.inl ())) +
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (u (Sum.inr ())) := by
    ext i
    rcases i with ⟨⟩ | ⟨⟩ <;> simp
  conv_lhs => rw [hu]
  rw [map_add, loopCellPathComparison_single_inl, loopCellPathComparison_single_inr]

/-- **The comparison commutes with the differentials**, for every Moore loop `γ` of every space:
the image `c_γ` of `e₁` bounds the image `([γ] - [1]) · [b]` of its attaching row. -/
theorem loopCellPathComparison_differential (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellPathComparison H R γ
        (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u) =
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopCellPathComparison H R γ u) := by
  refine ((forall_linearCombination_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_iff
    (pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule B b H R) _ _).2 ?_) u
  rintro (⟨⟨⟩⟩ | ⟨⟨⟩⟩)
  · simp
  · rw [loopCellCocycle_m_inr, Finsupp.linearCombination_single, Sum.elim_inl, sub_smul,
      point_smul_pathFromReflChain, one_smul, Sum.elim_inr, loopCellPathChain_differential]

/-- **The comparison commutes with the augmentations**: the augmentation of the image of `u` in
`C_*(P_b B; R)` is the augmentation of the coefficient of `e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathComparison (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R (loopCellPathComparison H R γ u) =
      loopCellAugmentation B b R u := by
  rw [loopCellPathComparison_apply, map_add, pathFromChainAugmentation_smul,
    pathFromChainAugmentation_smul, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_pathFromReflChain,
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathChain, _root_.mul_one, mul_zero, add_zero,
    loopCellAugmentation_apply]

end Comparison

section QuasiIso

universe u

variable {B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {H : Type*} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- **Brown's resolution of a circle is quasi-isomorphic to the chains on its based paths.** Let
`B` be aspherical at `b`, and let the class of the Moore loop `γ` generate the fundamental group
`π₁(B, b)` and have infinite order, as for a loop going once around a circle. Then the comparison
`TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison` from the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` to
`C_*(P_b B; R)` is a quasi-isomorphism: every relative cycle `(u, w)`, with `D u = 0` and
`c(u) = d w`, is a relative boundary `(D u', c(u') + d w')`.

Both augmentations are quasi-isomorphisms onto `R` and the comparison commutes with them. So `u`
has augmentation zero and is a boundary `D v`; then `w - c(v)` is a cycle, which up to a multiple
of `[b] = c(e₀)` has augmentation zero and is a boundary. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {γ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ))
    {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R} {w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0)
    (hw : loopCellPathComparison H R γ u = cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R w) :
    ∃ u' w', rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u' = u ∧
      loopCellPathComparison H R γ u' + cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R w' = w := by
  -- The cycle `u` has augmentation zero, so it is a boundary `D v`.
  have hε : loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0 := by
    rw [← cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathComparison (H := H), hw,
      cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_differential]
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero hB hgen
    hinf hu hε
  -- Then `z = w - c(v)` is a cycle; correct its augmentation `r` by `r e₀`, a cycle.
  set z := w - loopCellPathComparison H R γ v with hz
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ : ∃ r, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R z = r := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have he : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
      (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r)) = 0 := by
    have hs : Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R (loopChainAlgebra B b R) r) =
        r • (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) 1 : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) := by
      rw [Finsupp.smul_single, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
    rw [hs, map_smul, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl_one, smul_zero]
  have hdz : cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
      (z - loopCellPathComparison H R γ (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r))) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, hz, map_sub, ← hw, ← loopCellPathComparison_differential, hv,
      ← loopCellPathComparison_differential, he, map_zero, sub_self, sub_zero]
  have hεz : cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
      (z - loopCellPathComparison H R γ (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r))) = 0 := by
    have hεr : loopCellAugmentation B b R
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R (loopChainAlgebra B b R) r)) = r := by
      simp
    rw [map_sub, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_loopCellPathComparison, hεr, hr, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨w', hw'⟩ := exists_pathFromChainDifferential_eq_of_augmentation_eq_zero hdz hεz
  refine ⟨v + Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r), w', ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [map_add, hv, he, add_zero]
  · rw [hw', map_add, hz]
    abel

/-- **Brown's resolution of the circle is quasi-isomorphic to the chains on its based paths.** For
the complex unit circle, based at `1`, with its `1`-cell attached along the counterclockwise loop
`t ↦ exp(2πit)`, the comparison `TauCeti.loopCellPathComparison` with `C_*(P_1 S¹; R)` is a
quasi-isomorphism: every relative cycle is a relative boundary. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq
    {H : Type*} {R : Type} [CommRing R] {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R}
    {w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom Circle 1) H R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u = 0)
    (hw : loopCellPathComparison H R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop u =
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R w) :
    ∃ u' w', rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
        (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u' = u ∧
      loopCellPathComparison H R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop u' +
        cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R w' = w := by
  -- `MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom` takes the inverse of the path class of the loop.
  have hg : MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom (1 : Circle) Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop =
      (FundamentalGroup.fromPath (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk Circle.expLoop))⁻¹ := by
    rw [MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom_apply, Path.toPath_toMooreLoop]
  refine exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_and_loopCellPathComparison_add_eq
    (fun n ↦ inferInstance) ?_ ?_ hu hw
  · rw [hg, Subgroup.zpowers_inv, Circle.zpowers_fromPath_expLoop]
  · rw [hg, isOfFinOrder_inv_iff]
    exact Circle.not_isOfFinOrder_fromPath_expLoop

end QuasiIso

end TauCeti
